<h2 id="multilinear-algebra">Multilinear Algebra ◆</h2>
<p>In multilinear algebra, linear maps between vector spaces are generalized to maps over several vector spaces to several vector spaces at once, i.e., tensors. Multilinear algebra is rarely taught together with linear algebra, but could well be a subtopic in an advanced course, especially considering it is an important part of modern machine learning methodology. Multilinear algebra finds important use cases in differential geometry, as well as appearing naturally in calculus of several variables. Tensors are also integral to manybody methods like coupled-cluster theory or configuration-interaction theort.</p>
<p>Multilinear algebra is among the more useful topics for quantum chemists.</p>
